---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How It Works | Louisiana Credit Transfer Checker"
  description="How the free Louisiana credit transfer checker works, how Louisiana counselors join the list, and what we collect and never collect."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="block" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <h1>How the checker works</h1>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          Pick the college where the courses were taken, or will be taken,
          and the college the student wants to attend.
        </li>
        <li>
          Add courses from the dropdown lists. There is nothing to type and
          no account to create.
        </li>
        <li>
          See the answer course by course: what counts at the target
          college, what counts as an elective, and what does not transfer,
          with the published source behind each answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Compare two colleges side by side, check a transfer pathway, or
          run the eligibility and admission checks, all from the same
          published data.
        </li>
        <li>
          If something looks wrong, use the report an error link on the
          results. A Credit Transfer Pro reviews the published sources
          behind the answer, and the data is corrected when a source backs
          the correction.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/checker/">Start with the free checker</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Credits That Count turns Louisiana's published transfer rules into
        answers you can check. Every answer is built from official
        published sources: the Louisiana Board of Regents Course
        Articulation Matrix, the statewide common course catalog, college
        catalogs, and published admission standards, each dated and edition
        stamped.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is guidance, not an official ruling. Only the receiving college
        makes the final decision on how a credit applies, and requirements
        can change. The checker states what the published sources say today,
        and names its sources so you can verify every line with the
        college.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>For counselors</h2>
      <p>
        School counselors, independent counselors, tutoring centers,
        homeschool co-ops, and advising organizations can join the
        counselor list to hear first when counselor tools open. Our Credit
        Transfer Pros are former and current higher education administrators
        with experience in college student affairs, admissions, and student
        success, and the list is where counselor features are shaped.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/counselors/">Join the counselor list</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The checker runs on the colleges and courses you pick. We do not
        ask for transcripts, Social Security numbers, or student account
        passwords. If you write to us or join the counselor list, that
        information is used only to write back, and it is never sold.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the full <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for what we
        collect, what we never collect, and how to have your data deleted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="tagline-foot">Know before you go.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
